# Fixed LmxDec ABI: coefficient storage is 34 digits in every TU.
#
# The C form this replaces tested the macro before defining it --
# "#if defined(DECNUMDIGITS) / #if DECNUMDIGITS != 34 / #error ... / #else / #define
# DECNUMDIGITS 34 / #endif" -- because a different preexisting DECNUMDIGITS must be a
# compile error, not a resize.  L1 defines the macro; decNumber.h only defines its
# own default "if not defined", so with this header first 34 wins, and a TU that
# fixed a different value first gets the compiler's redefinition diagnostic.  What
# is NOT expressed here is a compile-time ""must equal 34"" test of an already
# defined macro: L1 has no conditional composition over a defined name (gap
# recorded, not worked around with raw C -- spec 1.9 forbids the hatch for this).
define: DECNUMDIGITS 34
